Reproduced: with a 400 ms refresh the sweep never moves in 300 ms. The second failure is just my new `angleAt` API that does not exist yet. Now the fix.

The sweep angle becomes a pure function of elapsed time, so a late or slow frame can never stall it, and the cache refresh runs beside it with a guard so refreshes do not pile up:

```ts
angleAt(now: number): number {
  const degreesPerMs = this.opts.degreesPerFrame / this.opts.frameIntervalMs;
  return (now - this.startedAt) * degreesPerMs;
}
```

In `TileCache` I fetch stale tiles in parallel batches of 6 with `Promise.allSettled`, so one failing tile no longer blocks the rest and keeps its old bitmap.

